MLX's CUDA quantized matmul has two kernels for a few rows of x: qmv, which
streams the whole weight matrix once per row, and the tiled qmm_sm80, which
reads it once but dequantizes into a tensor-core GEMM. On GB10 (sm_121) the
tiled kernel is the expensive one, so a speculative verify or a small batched
decode is faster as one weight read dotted with each row.

This adds that rows kernel. It is the default for up to 6 rows on GB10 and
stays off on every other chip, where the tiled kernel wins from 2 rows up.
MLX_CUDA_QMV_MAX_ROWS=<1..8> overrides either choice.

Drop this file and its step in build-mlx-linux.sh once lib/mlx-src includes
it.


